 ],
 "note": "r7.3 Atem session rules: the runtime reports a session's active rules; attachments with control get approval_rules on every change and after each sessions snapshot (view-only ones get none). Revoking one is a kind:\"approval_rule_revoke\" submission that needs only the control permission: with or without the lease, lease_epoch optional and ignored (here c2 revokes while c1 holds the lease, once without lease_epoch and once naming c1's epoch). A view-only attachment is forbidden; an inactive rule_id or another process_gen is stale_target; acquire is refused (the payload is exactly {rule_id}); nothing is recorded or dispatched for any of these. An active rule is dispatched to the runtime, completes when the worker dropped it, and the shorter list follows. A duplicate returns the recorded receipt; revoking again under a new request_id is stale_target. The holder's lease is untouched: it renews at the same epoch."
}
